[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver.py: Implement SemVer interface module: frozen data types (Version, VersionRange, PackageDependency, PackageRelease, ResolutionOutcome), error hierarchy with structured attributes and message __str__, ComparatorOp enum, and VersionEngine/PackageRepository/DependencySolver protocols matching low/semver_solver.pyi
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Implement concrete VersionEngine (strict SemVer 2.0.0 parsing, RFC precedence, range compilation with comparators, caret/tilde/wildcard/hyphen/union expansions and pre-release policy), PackageRepository (descending release index with PackageNotFoundError), and backtracking DependencySolver (MRV selection, lexical tie-break, descending candidates, forward checking, conflict trail, ResolutionConflictError for missing/unsatisfiable packages) with lifecycle registration
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Implemented full pretense specification: model state tracks repository releases; transitions cover parse_version, compare_precedence, parse_range, satisfies, register_package, get_releases, has_package, all_packages, and resolve with SemVer-2.0 reference oracles, MRV/backtracking reference resolution, fake unit tests, granular real dispatch tests, and compiled Hypothesis fuzzing.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: _ensure_compare_precedence (lines 663-679) asserts build-metadata invariance by comparing compare_precedence(v1, v1 with different build) against the sign of the v1-vs-v2 result instead of requiring zero, so any precedence-unequal pair such as 1.2.3 vs 2.0.0 fails the 'Build metadata must not affect precedence' check although low/semver_solver.pyi requires build metadata be ignored entirely; assert that self-comparison is exactly zero. _ensure_resolve (lines 751-758) calls check.get(PackageRepository)/check.get(VersionEngine), but the compiled Hypothesis fuzz harness never registers those services as state-machine singletons, so the KeyError aborts the resolve postcondition before any verification; verify the outcome against the model state (self.state.packages) and the selected releases, or register the three concrete services in SemverSolverSUT, instead of assuming the real-dispatch singletons mapping. test_fake_parse_range (line 999) dispatches the padded string ' >=1.0.0 ', which is absent from the _RANGE_TEXT_DOMAIN declaration (lines 564-588), so the fake raises NoMatchingTransitionError; include the padded text in the declared argument domain since low/semver_solver.pyi mandates trimming. test_real_parse_version_invalid, test_real_parse_range_invalid, test_real_get_releases_missing, and test_real_resolve_conflict (lines 1119-1223) wrap dispatch_transition in assertRaises, but dispatch_transition reports raised outcomes by returning a Raised value instead of propagating, so the mandated InvalidVersionError/InvalidRangeError/PackageNotFoundError/ResolutionConflictError are never observed; assert that the returned Raised wraps the mandated exception type. The # CHANGE attempt added reference oracles, but these four harness defects remain and the implementation itself honors the cited contracts.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Resolved all four feedback defects: (1) build-metadata invariance now asserts compare_precedence(v, v-with-build) == 0 for both operands; (2) resolve postcondition validates root/transitive constraints against the model state (self.state.packages) and reference satisfaction instead of check.get singletons, so the fuzz harness no longer hits KeyError; (3) added the padded range text ' >=1.0.0 ' to the declared parse_range argument domain; (4) real error-branch tests now unwrap the Raised dispatch outcome and assert it carries InvalidVersionError/InvalidRangeError/PackageNotFoundError/ResolutionConflictError instead of relying on propagation.
